BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (at $900 to $2,000 a year and weaker credit at several thousand. Brown adds that the premium also reflects financial) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (history, experience, and the surety company you pick [yiDO9s6ArZU @ 00:03:11]. Surety Bonds Direct also flags) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (prior bond claims as a price inflator, and says years of brokering can lower the rate. The bond renews yearly, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Manney warns that underwriters re-check credit at renewal, so a falling score means a bigger bill.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (The shopping playbook is aggressive and consistent. Brandon Scott's first bond came in at $3,000, paid as $750 a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (quarter. Scott admits they had great credit but accepted the first price without negotiating. They later reapplied at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (end of the term with a track record of paying carriers and cut the bill to $1,500 [lzC0i5OReRU @ 00:05:18]. Scott's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (rule is that the quote is not written in stone. Providers want to sell you a bond, and another company may beat the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (number if your credit is good, so negotiate, negotiate, negotiate. Scott also says to square up your personal credit first,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (because new brokers lack business credit and underwriters lean on personal credit [lzC0i5OReRU @ 00:04:05]. Mike) Tj ET
