BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 676.00 Tm (Section 4: Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 653.77 Tm (Matt Krause's most expensive lesson was tonal, not tactical: $750 lost on a load won with desperate energy, with no) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 638.55 Tm (leverage once the market spiked [AWq6iXM53f8 @ 00:00:00]. Early on, 100 calls a day produced about one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 623.32 Tm (meaningful conversation and Krause cut rates to roughly break even on loads. Competing on lowest rates delivered) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 608.10 Tm (razor-thin margins and clients who walked the moment another broker undercut, and five straight days of follow-ups) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.87 Tm (trained prospects to ignore the calls [LNT0OaH1J8s @ 00:01:55]. The rate request is its own trap: hand over a number) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 577.65 Tm (on "send me your rates" and "You are now in a bidding war," so Krause reframes around lead time, appointment-based) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 562.42 Tm (delivery and late penalties, then asks for the biggest operational challenge to sit as a consultant, not a vendor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 547.20 Tm ([ZG3bMHTCx1Y @ 00:05:13]. Jared's live call with a PVC pipe shipper in Bowling Green showed the same rot from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.97 Tm (the buyer's side: two carriers kept because they were "always the cheapest," and bidding wars putting too many trucks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 516.75 Tm (on site [gwNcz_V8JZ0 @ 00:21:21]. The symptoms Krause tags as commission breath, speaking fast, ums, upspeak) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 501.52 Tm (and jumping to price, signal a thin pipeline, and the cure Krause teaches is enough pipeline that power comes from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 486.30 Tm (indifference: there to help, not to beg.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.07 Tm (The first load is a test, and Dennis Brown says shippers grade it on a scorecard of pickups, deliveries, damage claims) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.85 Tm (and rejected loads [BCLv7SfCxIo @ 00:30:49]. Overcommitting is how new brokers flunk it: offered five) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 440.62 Tm (Buffalo-to-Atlanta loads, take three, because committing to five and covering three makes you "a loser." The quieter) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 425.40 Tm (failure is the one Krause calls the ghost broker approach: over 80% of brokers fail to win repeat business after the first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.17 Tm (load because they send "your load is booked" and vanish, leaving the shipper without the carrier, the phone number or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 394.95 Tm (the arrival time, so the shipper starts calling other brokers [Bdydc4rCcVs @ 00:00:17]. The fix is a two-paragraph) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 379.72 Tm (handover email naming the carrier, pickup window, equipment, driver and the driver's direct line, then a capacity nudge) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 364.50 Tm (for loads in the next week or two. Dennis's pet food account shows the payoff of the ask: after the first $150 load,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.27 Tm ("When's the next load on that lane shipping?" won the next one on the spot, and the account grew to about $20,000 a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.05 Tm (year in profit for 5+ years [knW5LzcUJIw @ 00:04:16]. Kevin Hill of FreightWaves adds a staffing trap: new reps') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.82 Tm (first freight is often "horrible," so start them in carrier sales or ops [iOTP-SdRDb4 @ 00:43:49].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 303.60 Tm (Cash and bandwidth break brokerages before the phone does. John Ferguson launched from a basement, invoicing at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.37 Tm (night, paying carriers via Zelle out of a personal account while customers paid in 30 days, and asked underwriters) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.15 Tm (mid-call for $900 to $1,500 in credit because top loads paid about $2k [PyjJOzy-a2s @ 00:17:55]. Recycling shippers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 257.92 Tm (in that early book cared only about rate. Jared of eCarrierCheck admitted on a live call that he failed to ask about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 242.70 Tm (payment terms, with fuel at $5 a gallon putting a 300-gallon fill near $1,500 for the carrier, and his verdict on a shipper) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.47 Tm (that won't work with him was "I'd probably find another shipper" [gwNcz_V8JZ0 @ 00:59:07]. Kevin Hill warns that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 212.25 Tm (cradle-to-grave service eats selling time: cross-border Mexico work once meant eight hours with no sales calls, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.02 Tm (is why Axle's team leaders cover check calls so a rep can "go sell for an hour" [iOTP-SdRDb4 @ 00:36:55]. Dennis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 181.80 Tm (Brown flags two more traps: the lowest RFQ bidder often cannot cover the volume and rejects the tender, so placing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 166.57 Tm (second to fourth wins, and LinkedIn automation violates terms of service and can cost the account entirely) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.35 Tm ([90xG4lQaA6Q @ 00:46:54]. His bidding rule is to bid only the 20 to 40 lanes you are actually good at.) Tj ET
