BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (broker is named, and a Minneapolis to Elk River post paying $2,500 for 32 miles was an instant scam call) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm ([3dI5z6SHDPc @ 00:14:19]. On paper, Cana checks whether the pro number font differs from the rest of the header,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (whether the email domain matches the real brokerage, and whether shipper and receiver codes are four-character) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (alphanumerics, which signal an Amazon load that is a scam if it is not moving through the Relay app [3dI5z6SHDPc @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (00:24:56]. A Gmail address triggers questions every time; Cana has verified only two legitimate brokers using Gmail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (out of roughly 60,000. Behavioral tells include one-line rate cons with no fine print, a broker demanding the bill of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (lading at pickup, check-in instructions under another carrier's name, and status demands at arrival, check-in, loading,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (and paperwork. Freight 360's Nate Cross adds that a too-good rate usually means the carrier plans to rebroker, take) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (quick pay, and vanish, leaving the broker to pay the second carrier again [gnxgKnnz6Jw @ 00:02:20].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (For brokers, the working stack layers vetting software over physical proof. Nate Cross runs Highway at the Freight 360) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (brokerage for inspection history, registered equipment, community reports, and an ELD-fed map of equipment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (locations, then makes GPS tracking mandatory for the full load when fraud is suspected; most fraudsters quit once) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (challenged for tracking or an ELD download before payment [uGu6NcZkt28 @ 00:01:57]. Cross also demands photos) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (or video at the shipper showing equipment, the driver's face, registration, driver's license, and the MC on the truck) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (door, zooming in for doctored images, and withholds the PO or pickup number until identity and location are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (confirmed. QuickScope automates that gate: the driver gets a text, takes a one-time photo inside a 2m geofence, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (character recognition checks the company name, MC, and DOT before pickup details release automatically) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm ([uGu6NcZkt28 @ 00:03:45]. Hank Seaton estimates two-thirds to three-quarters of truckload shipments move without) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (the carrier's name on the paperwork [jnoJihiGSEA @ 00:25:28]. His protocol: put the authorized carrier's name on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (bill of lading, send that name to the consignor at booking, show the contracting broker as the send-freight-bill-to party,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (and require the driver to present credentials, including a driver's license, satisfactory to the consignor [jnoJihiGSEA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (00:26:07].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (Carriers get their own checklist. Cana tells them to call the corporate office of any medium or large brokerage, found) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm (through the DAT directory, to confirm the load number, the lane, and that they are listed as carrier of record; with small) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (shops, ask the shipper which broker it uses, but never talk money, because that edges into back solicitation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm ([3dI5z6SHDPc @ 00:29:21]. Cana also recommends drivers sign over a colored rubber stamp carrying the MC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (number, carrier name, and driver name, so a scammer cannot hide the real carrier or forge a clean receiver signature) Tj ET
